# Izi.FluentData code style

Baseline: Microsoft's C# coding conventions and .NET Framework Design Guidelines
(https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/csharp/fundamentals/coding-style/coding-conventions,
https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/standard/design-guidelines/). Enforced by the root `.editorconfig`.
Rules below are project-specific additions or clarifications. Comments in English.

## Layout
- File-scoped namespaces; one top-level type per file; partials split by topic (`TransformerRules.DateTime.cs`).
- 4-space indent, Allman braces, braces always (even single-line `if`).
- `using` directives outside the namespace, `System.*` first.
- Modifier order per .NET defaults: accessibility, `static`, `readonly` (`private static readonly`).
- Explicit accessibility modifiers on all non-interface members.
- Member order: constants, static fields, fields, constructors, properties, public methods, private methods, nested types.

## Naming (Framework Design Guidelines)
- PascalCase: types, methods, properties, events, constants, static readonly fields.
- `_camelCase`: private instance fields. `camelCase`: locals and parameters.
- Interfaces start with `I`; generic type parameters start with `T`.
- Async methods end in `Async`; internal async continuations end in `SlowAsync`.
- No abbreviations or Hungarian notation; built-in rule factories are named after the rule (`NotNull`, `MaxLength`).

## Language usage
- `var` when the type is apparent; explicit type otherwise.
- Collection expressions (`[]`) and target-typed `new()` where clear.
- Language features limited to what all target frameworks support (C# 12 with `net8.0;net10.0`) unless `LangVersion` is pinned.
- Guard public arguments with `ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull` / `ArgumentOutOfRangeException.ThrowIf*`.

## Documentation
- XML docs (`<summary>`, `<param>`, `<returns>`, `<exception>`) on every public member; `GenerateDocumentationFile` on.
- `//` comments explain *why*, not what. No `#region`.

## Performance (hard rule)
- Passing validation/transformation must not allocate: shared empty results, lazy `??=` lists, message delegates invoked only on failure.
- Sync fast path via `ValueTask.IsCompletedSuccessfully`, then a `SlowAsync` tail; `ConfigureAwait(false)` on every await (CA2007).
- Indexed `for` over `List<T>` in hot loops, consistent between fast and slow paths. No LINQ in rule predicates.

## Public API
- Breaking public changes only in a major version; collect wanted renames for the next major.
